---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import About from '../components/About.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Sponsors from '../components/Sponsors.astro';

const organizers = (await getCollection('authors'))
	.filter((entry) => entry.id.startsWith('en/'))
	.map((entry) => entry.data);
---

<PageLayout title="About Summit" description="The people and partners bringing Summit to Morelia.">
	<section class="content-shell py-12 space-y-14">
		<About lang="en" />

		<section class="grid gap-8 border-b border-border pb-14 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.25fr)_minmax(16rem,0.75fr)]" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
			<div class="space-y-5">
				<p class="eyebrow m-0">The gathering</p>
				<h1 id="about-heading" class="m-0 text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">A conference for the work that happens after the keynote.</h1>
				<p class="m-0 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">Summit is a small conference for people who make the web: the designers mapping a useful flow, the developers keeping a service dependable, the writers giving an interface its voice, and the teams making room for all of that work to happen.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">We bring those perspectives together because the most durable digital work is rarely the result of one discipline working alone. It comes from honest trade-offs, shared language, and the willingness to examine how a decision will feel to the person on the other side of the screen.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">Across the program, speakers share the details behind their practice: what they tried, what changed their mind, and what they would do differently next time. The aim is not a catalogue of finished answers. It is a more useful conversation about how to make better ones.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="space-y-5 border-l-0 border-border pt-1 lg:border-l lg:pl-8">
				<p class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">Built for attention, not acceleration.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">The schedule leaves space between sessions for questions, chance conversations, and a proper break. Two rooms keep the program varied without turning the day into a race from one headline to the next.</p>
				<p class="m-0 leading-relaxed text-muted">Morelia gives the gathering a human scale: a walkable historic center, generous public spaces, and a venue made for being in the same room. Come for the talks, stay for the conversations that continue after them.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="space-y-6" aria-labelledby="organizers-heading">
			<header class="max-w-2xl space-y-2">
				<p class="eyebrow m-0">Organizers</p>
				<h1 id="organizers-heading" class="m-0 text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">The people behind Summit</h1>
				<p class="m-0 text-muted">A small local team shaping a thoughtful, practical gathering for the open web community.</p>
			</header>
			<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
				{organizers.map((organizer) => <Card title={organizer.name} eyebrow={organizer.role} description={organizer.bio} image={organizer.avatar} imageAlt={organizer.name} />)}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-y border-border py-10" aria-labelledby="sponsors-heading">
			<div class="max-w-2xl space-y-3">
				<p class="eyebrow m-0">Sponsors</p>
				<h2 id="sponsors-heading" class="m-0 text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink">Help make Summit possible</h2>
				<p class="m-0 text-muted">Sponsorship supports accessible tickets, a welcoming venue, and the practical details that make an in-person event work. Partner opportunities will be announced soon.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="mt-8">
				<Sponsors />
			</div>
		</section>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
